  "articleBody": "It can be tough to know exactly when a home repair crosses the line from a DIY project to something that really needs a professional touch, especially for seniors. Think about anything that impacts safety or mobility first. If there's an issue with plumbing, like a persistent leak that could cause water damage or a slippery floor, that's definitely a pro job. The same goes for electrical problems; flickering lights or outlets that aren't working right can be really dangerous and need an expert to prevent fire hazards or shocks. Structural issues, even small cracks in walls or ceilings, shouldn't be ignored either, as they could signal bigger problems. And, of course, if you're looking to add accessibility features like grab bars or ramps, you want them installed correctly and up to code for maximum safety. Even if you're handy, some jobs require specific tools, permits, or knowledge of building codes that only a qualified professional from a company like HH Remodeling LLC would have. Don't risk your safety or the integrity of your home trying to tackle something beyond your comfort zone. Give us a call at 303-505-0866, we serve the greater Denver area.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}